   "in_list_view": 1,
   "label": "Balance Amount",
   "read_only": 1
  },
  {
   "description": "posting_date plus a same-day sub-second offset (Opening Balance always gets the earliest offset, then each other same-day entry by insertion order) — exists only so the single-column default list sort can put the newest entry first and Opening Balance last even when a real transaction shares its date. The Report/List View's Sort By control always sends exactly one column, so a passbook-correct order needs one field that already encodes the full precedence; posting_date alone (a Date, no time component) can't break same-day ties. Recomputed alongside balance_amount by refresh_current_balance().",
